 48		blobFetcher     BlobFetchFunc
 49		refFetcher      RefFetchFunc
 50		remoteRefLister RemoteRefListFunc
 51	
 52		// fetchFailureMu guards fetchFailure: the first transport-level ref-fetch
 53		// failure, memoized for the store's lifetime so a loop over N missing refs
 54		// (e.g. a stop hook finalizing every checkpoint of a turn) pays a dead —
 55		// or too-slow-for-the-budget — network once instead of N times. Genuine
 56		// remote absence is per-ref and
 57		// is never memoized. The memo never clears — safe because every
 58		// fetcher-wired store today is opened per command/hook invocation; a
 59		// long-lived fetcher-wired store would need an expiry before reusing this.
 60		fetchFailureMu sync.Mutex
